  "citation": "(1981) 1 Sri LR 488",
  "statement": "The Rent Act does not apply to subletting of premises that occurred before its commencement date.",
  "supporting_quote": "1. Section 10(7) of the Rent Act is a bar to a suit on sub letting where the premises had been sublet prior to the date of commencement of the Rent Act (13.1.1972) so long as that person continues, to be a subtenant of the premises so sub-let. The word \"that person\" in s. 10(7) of the Rent Act mean the sub-tenant and not the tenant. 2. Section 28 of the Rent Act Provides for the ejectment of a tenant of any residential premises who has ceased to occupy same for six months. This section does not apply to business premises as here",
